{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-ey:000001:issue_created:bob-cli-ey:64d37e68ac1a553194081269175795e8e83e1efd6c25a44ef33875f3b018b9c3","timestamp":"2026-10-31T16:52:03Z","actor":"bbugyi200.apollo.research.2x.linker.w0","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"bob-cli-ey","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"bob-cli-ey","title":"Capture drawers and % directives","status":"open","issue_type":"plan","tier":"epic","parent_id":null,"owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-10-31T16:52:03Z","created_by":"bbugyi200.apollo.research.2x.linker.w0","updated_at":"2026-10-31T16:52:03Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"Bob's capture language reads as three rules: @ says where, # names a place or a type, and % says how. `Text @note+id#drawer [#type]` files a note in a task drawer, creating the drawer when it is missing and optionally retyping the task in the same transaction. `%c`, `%n`, `%t`, and `%l` replace trailing `#`, `%`, `@@template:`, and `URL %`. Typing `#`, `%`, or `@note+id#` in Bob Mac Capture opens a bob-described menu with nothing preselected. Every retired form is deleted outright, with no aliases.","design":"plan:202610/capture_drawers_and_directives.md","model":"","is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","creation_reason":"Approved epic plan plan:202610/capture_drawers_and_directives.md requests this work","dependencies":[]}}}
